course: dictionary
lesson: 9498
title: One word, many steps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Step can mean a movement of your foot, a flat part of a staircase, or one part of a process. The sentence around it tells you which meaning to use. «The stairs have twelve steps» is about the flat parts, but «To find the answer, undo each step» is about parts of a process.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. In «The Zebra and the Giraffe step into the striped and blotchy shadows», step means to move by lifting your foot and putting it down. If your meaning fits the sentence and makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: Look for small clues like the words next to step. «Step by step» means slowly, one part after another. «Watch your step» means be careful where you put your feet. «Stepbrother» is a family word, not a stair word, because the step means a family joined by a new marriage.
fact: A step can be one movement of your foot when you walk.
fact: Steps are the flat parts of stairs that you walk up.
fact: A step can also be one part of a process, such as the first step of a recipe.
fact: To step means to move by lifting your foot and putting it down.
fact: «Step by step» means slowly, one part after another.
exercise: «The Zebra and the Giraffe step into the striped and blotchy shadows.» What does step mean here? | Count the stripes slowly | Shout loudly | Stop and fall asleep | *Move by lifting a foot and putting it down
exercise: «To find how many there were at the start, begin at the end and undo each step in the opposite order.» In this sentence, what is a step? | *One part of the working | A pair of shoes | A flat part of stairs | One movement of your foot
exercise: Ravi says, «My stepbrother lives with us now.» What is a stepbrother? | A brother who is taller than you | A brother who likes stairs | *A brother from a new marriage in the family | A brother who walks to school with you
test: «The stairs have twelve steps.» In this sentence, what are the steps? | One movement of your foot | One part of a recipe | *The flat parts you walk up | A slow way of moving
test: «Do it step by step.» What does step by step mean? | Without using your feet | Only on Tuesdays | Very quickly, all at once | *Slowly, one part after another
exam: What does stepped mean in «she nearly stepped in front of a van»? | Sang a song | Hid behind a tree | Stopped the bus with her hand | *Moved by lifting her foot and putting it down
